      },
      "question": "Read the extract and answer the questions.\n\n*The fog comes*\n*on little cat feet.*\n**\n*It sits looking*\n*over harbor and city*\n*on silent haunches*\n*and then moves on.*\n\n(i) Name the poem and the poet.\n\n(ii) To what is the fog compared?\n\n(iii) What does 'haunches' mean?\n\n(iv) Name the device used throughout.\n\n(v) What does 'moves on' suggest?",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "answer_steps": [
        "(i) Fog, Carl Sandburg.",
        "(ii) A cat.",
        "(iii) The back legs and hips of an animal, on which it sits.",
        "(iv) Extended metaphor.",
        "(v) The fog lifts and disappears silently."
      ],
      "marking_scheme": [
        "(i) 1 mark",
        "(ii) 1 mark",
        "(iii) 1 mark",
        "(iv) 1 mark",
        "(v) 1 mark"
      ]
